life for so many feels like it's on hold  but helplessness and uncertainty have  haunted nick talbert for the past  three years this rural farm in ohio  is not where he expected to be living it  was like my entire future had just been  taken away  in one moment over social media for no  good reason  that moment was a tweet by president  trump in july 2017  stating that transgender people would no  longer be allowed to serve  in the u.s military including nick  this ban treats transgender people as  lesser people  this ban implies that we are not as  worthy we are not as capable and none of  that is true at all  so this one was taken during a weekend  field training exercise  at the time of the tweet nick was  planning a future serving his country  when his president took that future away  nick decided to fight  in court trump's policy was delayed  but not defeated this has been an  absolute roller coaster for me  emotionally  physically in my personal life  there are just so many unknowns tell me  about your reaction when you found out  that biden had won  it was like a huge sigh of relief for me  i'm proud of the coalition we put  together the broadest  and most diverse coalition in history  gay straight transgender white latino  asian  joe biden has promised to allow  transgender people to serve openly  in the military and increase protections  for the lgbtq  community discrimination is still  rampant  in this country and lgbtq people  particularly transgender and gender  non-conforming people  are often the targets of that i don't  think it is going to take long  at all for people to feel the effect of  an administration that  actually cares about all americans  but biden's ambitions could be derailed  by two  upcoming elections that will determine  which party controls the senate  the house has already passed legislation  that would make any kind of  discrimination against the lgbtq  community illegal but republican senate  leaders stop the bill from progressing  any further biden has said that passing  the equality act  would be a priority in his first 100  days in office  but he needs the senate on side and if  republicans hold the power  they may be reluctant to support a law  that could anger many deeply religious  americans  without blanket legislation condemning  discrimination against the lgbtq  community  the courts have to decide whose rights  are most at risk  and thanks to president trump the top  court in the country  has a much more conservative lineup i  think that when the bride administration  makes its policies it's going to have to  be aware that  there's a judiciary that has a very  broad view of what the free exercise of  religion means  and so if they do certain things they  would have to worry that their  decisions would be overwritten by the  courts but possible battles in the  courts or  congress will not dampen nick's dreams  i'm really hoping that with the new  presidency  we can finally get some solid answers  and i can finally start to move on and  be a real adult  he hopes he won't have to wait too long  becky kochel sky news lisbon ohio
 

